    "can_train_24h_forecasting": false,
    "justification": "Only 67 reliably dated historical landslide events exist in the authoritative NASA catalog within Meghalaya. A supervised 24-hour binary prediction model across a 25x40 or fine-resolution daily grid requires hundreds of temporally distributed positive events paired with continuous antecedent rainfall records to avoid severe overfitting and unresolvable class imbalance. Therefore, scientific honesty dictates that we construct a Static Landslide Susceptibility Model (using terrain factors: elevation, slope, aspect, curvature, and lithological/topographic wetness) coupled with antecedent rainfall thresholding (heuristic/empirical trigger curves), rather than claiming to have trained an unvalidated supervised next-day event probability model.",
    "recommendation": "Build static geomorphic landslide susceptibility mapping first; formulate dynamic hazard as empirical Rainfall-Triggered Susceptibility index."
  },
